# Overlay & Rendering

## Thread model

- **Main tick** (`RadarApp`): memory reads, hotkeys, builds `RenderContext`, publishes via volatile/ref swap.
- **ImGui thread** (STA, `ImGuiRadarOverlay`): consumes `RenderContext`, draws only — **no** `MemoryReader` calls in `Render()`.
- **World thread** (`WorldReaderLoop`): heavy entity/terrain walk → `WorldSnapshot`.

Never block the render thread on memory I/O or pathfinding.

## RenderContext / WorldSnapshot

- Immutable-ish snapshots passed to render; use `Array.Empty<T>()` for cleared state.
- World-rate data (entities, terrain, paths) from `WorldSnapshot`; frame-rate data (player, map lock) from live frame.
- Item labels / HP bars: spec from world tick; overlay may re-read **live position only** for smooth follow.

## Draw policy

- Skip overlay when game unfocused unless `AlwaysShowOverlay`.
- Respect per-layer toggles (`ShowPathWorld`, `ShowPathMap`, `MapOverlayDrawPolicy`, etc.).
- Style from `RadarSettings` — colors, sizes, opacity, shapes via `IconAtlas` / `SpriteIconRef`.
- Anchor to game **client rect** (`GetClientRect` + `ClientToScreen`), not outer window rect.

## ImGui conventions

- `ImGuiConfigFlags.NoMouseCursorChange` — don't steal cursor from game.
- `OverlayVSync` user-tunable; record segment timings in `OverlayRenderMetrics` when adding heavy draw passes.

## Settings panel UI (accordion pattern)

Dense tabs (Radar, Performance, Entities, HP Bars, Flask, Atlas, Hotkeys) use **collapsible accordions**, not always-open section walls or nested `BeginChild` panels.

- **Helpers:** `ImGuiTheme.BeginAccordionSection(id, title, subtitle?, defaultOpen)` + `EndAccordionSection(open)` — full-width `CollapsingHeader` (`SpanAvailWidth | FramePadding`), muted subtitle only when expanded, light indent for controls.
- **Tab scroll:** one `BeginTabScroll` child per tab (`Vector2.Zero` + vertical scrollbar). **Never** nest extra `BeginChild(0,0)` section panels inside tabs — that collapsed content in the past.
- **Defaults:** all sections start **collapsed** when you open settings or switch tabs (`CollapseSectionsOnNextDraw` + `SetNextItemOpen(false)`). Expand state persists while you stay on that tab.
- **Tab ownership:** app-wide perf (FPS cap, Hz, smoothing, metrics HUD, UI font) lives **only** on the **Performance** tab — not duplicated on Radar. Radar may show a one-line cross-link to Performance.
- **Nested lists:** large inventories (entity tiers, atlas tags) may use inner `CollapsingHeader` or fixed-height `BeginChild` **inside** an open accordion — not as the tab's outer layout.
- **Startup launcher** (`StartupMenuOverlay`) keeps flat `SectionHeader` — fewer controls, no accordion needed.

```csharp
bool open = ImGuiTheme.BeginAccordionSection("MapDisplay", "Map display", "…");
if (open) { /* controls */ }
ImGuiTheme.EndAccordionSection(open);
```

New settings groups → new accordion section with stable `id`; wire in ImGui + dashboard per `config-settings.mdc`.

## Assets

- Built-in SVG icons → `IconLibrary.MaterializeTo` on first run; user overrides in `icons/`.
- Texture atlas via `IconAtlas` / `TextureRegistry` — don't load per-frame.
